payload.message:
That last step is straightforward: after the RemoteHost streams the final `FileChunk` with `is_last = true`, call `asio::async_shutdown` (if you want a graceful TLS shutdown) and then close the socket. In pseudocode:

```cpp
void FileTransferSession::SendChunks() {
    if (offset_ >= fileSize_) {
        SendFinalChunk();
        return;
    }
    // send next chunk...
}

void FileTransferSession::SendFinalChunk() {
    FileChunk last{ .sequence = seq_, .is_last = true, ... };
    async_write(stream_, buffer(last),
        [this](auto ec, auto) {
            if (!ec) {
                stream_.async_shutdown([this](auto ec) {
                    stream_.lowest_layer().close();
                });
            } else {
                HandleError(ec);
            }
        });
}
```

This ensures the dedicated Port 2 connection is torn down immediately after the transfer completes, matching the “close connection after transfer” requirement.

